        "type": "markdown-mermaid",
        "title": "Selected turning points, not a complete succession of states",
        "content": "```mermaid\ntimeline\n  title Selected medieval turning points in CE\n  821 : Tahirid governorship begins in Khorasan\n  873 : Saffarids take Nishapur from the Tahirids\n  1040 : Seljuks defeat the Ghaznavids at Dandanakan\n  1258 : Mongol capture of Baghdad ends Abbasid rule there\n  1295 : Ilkhan Ghazan converts to Islam\n  1370 : Timur establishes power in Transoxiana\n  1405 : Timur dies and succession reshapes his empire\n```",
        "summary": "These events orient the reader across several overlapping political worlds. They do not imply that each dynasty governed the same territory or immediately replaced every predecessor.",
